One pending notification retained per seat already existed. Fixed-order retries let hot first seats reclaim each freed credit, leaving three watched seats with zero admissions in 12,409/12,409/12,408 attempts during stop-to-timeout.
Change: Actor keeps last_notified_seat; only successful notify advances it. tick_seats starts after that seat with wraparound, preserving the same per-seat tick body. No additional queue or runtime task.
Production channel remains 128 slots. No wire, frame/body budget, raw FIFO, lifecycle, Exit, generation, ring, capture, replay, checkpoint or PTY rate change.
Code: crates/bbt-supervisor/src/supervisor.rs Actor field/init, tick_seats extraction/rotation, notify success cursor, private counterexample test.
Invariant: .bboxy/invariants/no-seat-starves.md active with full unit-test check; README row matches. --lib plus full module path and the one-passed assertion prevent zero-test false success.
The default fixture owns two /bin/sleep children and a capacity-1 local channel; it returns one credit per sweep while replenishing the first seat. No clock assertion. Second seat receives the next credit; hot-seat sequences remain FIFO.

